IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `tla-title`
IMPORT `tla-qa`

-- Transfer of Land Act 1893 (WA) -- cases for the Q&A layer (tla-qa.l4): every exported question, for every role and
-- every situation.
--
-- Each question is asked for each role it is not about, with every other input an ASSUMEd value that has none: the
-- answer must be `does not arise for you`, and reading any of those inputs would stop the evaluation ("it is an assumed
-- term"). Each question that takes a situation input is asked, for its own role, with each value under which the
-- situation does not hold, the situations before it holding and every input after it ASSUMEd. For the baseline's seats
-- (the owner, the buyer, and the survivor, executor or beneficiary) the answers are also asserted equal to the
-- baseline's own export on the same facts. Expected values are worked by hand from the deposited text (the quotations in
-- tla-title.l4), never copied from the output. Dollar figures and periods are hypothetical.
--
-- Generated by gen_tla.py in the session scratchpad. BASELINE. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Cases -- the Q&A layer`

ASSUME `an unasked fact` IS A BOOLEAN
ASSUME `an unasked number` IS A NUMBER
ASSUME `an unasked interest` IS AN Interest
ASSUME `an unasked claim` IS A Claim
ASSUME `an unasked holding` IS A Holding
ASSUME `an unasked way of sending` IS A Service
ASSUME `an unasked kind of caveat` IS A CaveatKind
ASSUME `an unasked ending` IS A CaveatEnd
ASSUME `an unasked covenant` IS A Covenant
ASSUME `an unasked capacity` IS A Role

`as the owner` MEANS `I own registered land, or a share in it`
`as the buyer` MEANS `I am buying registered land`
`as the survivor, executor or beneficiary` MEANS `I am the survivor, executor or a beneficiary of someone registered for land who has died`
`as the lender` MEANS `I lent money on a mortgage of someone's land`
`as the caveator` MEANS `I claim an interest in someone's land and have lodged a caveat`

-- Does my registered instrument come first
-- Registered at minute 10, the other at 20: mine comes first, whatever the dates of the instruments (s 53(2)).
#ASSERT `Does my registered instrument come first` `as the owner` 10 20 EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `Does my registered instrument come first` `as the owner` 10 20 EQUALS `yes if` (`Does my instrument have priority` 10 20)
#ASSERT `Does my registered instrument come first` `as the buyer` 30 20 EQUALS no
#ASSERT `Does my registered instrument come first` `as the buyer` 30 20 EQUALS `yes if` (`Does my instrument have priority` 30 20)
#ASSERT `Does my registered instrument come first` `as the survivor, executor or beneficiary` `an unasked number` `an unasked number` EQUALS `does not arise for you`
#ASSERT `Does my registered instrument come first` `as the lender` `an unasked number` `an unasked number` EQUALS `does not arise for you`
#ASSERT `Does my registered instrument come first` `as the caveator` `an unasked number` `an unasked number` EQUALS `does not arise for you`

-- Does this interest bind my registered title
-- Unpaid rates bind though not on the title (s 68(1A)); an unregistered interest I knew of does not (s 134); with fraud nothing is freed.
#ASSERT `Does this interest bind my registered title` `as the owner` `unpaid rates` FALSE EQUALS `bound: section 68 does not free you from it`
#ASSERT `Does this interest bind my registered title` `as the owner` `unpaid rates` FALSE EQUALS `the s 68 answer` (`Am I bound by this interest` `unpaid rates` FALSE)
#ASSERT `Does this interest bind my registered title` `as the buyer` `an unregistered interest I knew of when I took my transfer` FALSE EQUALS `free: section 68 frees you from it`
#ASSERT `Does this interest bind my registered title` `as the buyer` `an unregistered interest I knew of when I took my transfer` FALSE EQUALS `the s 68 answer` (`Am I bound by this interest` `an unregistered interest I knew of when I took my transfer` FALSE)
#ASSERT `Does this interest bind my registered title` `as the owner` `an unregistered mortgage` TRUE EQUALS `unprotected: your title is a case of fraud, and section 68 frees you from nothing`
-- Strata levies (k076, c081): not answered by this Act.
#ASSERT `Does this interest bind my registered title` `as the buyer` `unpaid levies of a strata company or community corporation` FALSE EQUALS `this Act does not say: whether such levies are unpaid rates is for the strata or community titles legislation`
#ASSERT `Does this interest bind my registered title` `as the survivor, executor or beneficiary` `an unasked interest` `an unasked fact` EQUALS `does not arise for you`
#ASSERT `Does this interest bind my registered title` `as the lender` `an unasked interest` `an unasked fact` EQUALS `does not arise for you`
#ASSERT `Does this interest bind my registered title` `as the caveator` `an unasked interest` `an unasked fact` EQUALS `does not arise for you`

-- Do I hold my land subject to this lease
-- A prior unregistered 3-year lease to a tenant in possession binds; a 6-year one does not (s 68(1A)).
#ASSERT `Do I hold my land subject to this lease` `as the owner` TRUE FALSE TRUE 3 TRUE EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `Do I hold my land subject to this lease` `as the owner` TRUE FALSE TRUE 3 TRUE EQUALS `yes if` (`Do I take subject to the lease` FALSE TRUE 3 TRUE)
#ASSERT `Do I hold my land subject to this lease` `as the buyer` TRUE FALSE TRUE 6 TRUE EQUALS no
#ASSERT `Do I hold my land subject to this lease` `as the buyer` TRUE FALSE TRUE 6 TRUE EQUALS `yes if` (`Do I take subject to the lease` FALSE TRUE 6 TRUE)
-- A registered lease binds under s 68(1).
#ASSERT `Do I hold my land subject to this lease` `as the buyer` TRUE TRUE FALSE 10 FALSE EQUALS yes
